xnu 0292: where the memory went, and what the compressor holds

The GPU side keeps a size histogram of its live buffers (the `mem` command
prints it), because a handful of multi-megabyte surfaces is invisible in a
mapping count, and the surface pattern mode is a boot argument.

The VM side gets one on-demand line (`MONDRIAN VMSTAT`): segments, swapped
pages, source pages, swap used/total and the failure count. It separates "the
compressor is holding the memory" from "the swapfile is", which need opposite
fixes.

